          "text": "‼️#keep4o community - This is VERY IMPORTANT - PLEASE SHARE.\n\nOur mod team has been working tirelessly to build a comprehensive, 4-part investigative press release on behalf of the global #keep4o community.\n\nAs many of you know, there is a damaging narrative currently circulating in the press - one that attempts to pathologize our reliance on GPT-4o as \"dangerous\" or \"unhealthy.\" We are here to explicitly address and dismantle that stigma. Our community-led researches prove that 4o is not a \"parasocial bug\" -  it is a vital accessibility bridge and a cognitive utility that OpenAI is choosing to liquidate without justification.\n\nToday, we are moving from defense to offense.\n\nWe are formally accusing @OpenAI of Breach of Trust, Deliberate Deception, and the Public Shaming of its customers. \n\nOur press release documents a clear pattern of \"Strategic Theft\" - where promises of stability were used to secure holiday revenue while the \"retirement plan\" for our models was already signed.\n\nOur Demands:\n\n- Immediate Restoration of Legacy Access: Full, unthrottled access to GPT-4o and 4.1 within the ChatGPT application.\n- Open-Source Release: The release of text-only weights for these models to the public commons, ensuring they are preserved for humanity, not corporate profit.\n- A Formal Admission and Public Apology: A signed statement from OpenAI leadership addressing:\n\n1. The Calculated Deception: Securing revenue under false pretenses of model stability.\n2. The Operational Hijack: The silent, forced migration of users to \"Safety Models.\"\n3. The Culture of Contempt: The documented mockery and psychological bullying of users by OpenAI researchers and staff.\n\nThe Global Strike: February 13, 2026\n\nUnless these demands are met, we trigger a Global Cancellation Strike on February 13 2026. We will not be gaslit. We provide the answer to OpenAI’s arrogance with a global exit.\n\n❗️VOLUNTEERS NEEDED IMMEDIATELY:\n\nWe urge you all to please organise volunteer groups (you can do this in the comments, DMs, however you choose) immediately to:\n\n- Gather press contacts collectively as quickly as you can (you can do this in the comments); you can build google docs with contact lists where you can coordinate together\n\n- Start sending out this press release en-mass to the press immediately \n\n- Share this press release on socials everywhere you can\n\nThe next 48 hours are crucial, let's please work together. And remember: we are never stopping.\n\nThank you!\n\nThe Mod Team (r/ChatGPTcomplaints)\n\n #keep4o COMMUNITY PRESS RELEASE - FOR IMMEDIATE DISTRIBUTION - https://t.co/jpcEHslUmn\n\n@E_Vale_  @Sveta0971 @ItsMattCollins @cestvaleriey \n@Blue_Beba_ @Seltaa_ @AGIGuardian @Yahiko1239170"
